From 206ccd25f1a178372f4dc9ed23b7982abdf5db2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Mar 2025 20:02:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1670/1695] clk: stm32: fix management of set_rate and
 determine_rate

When .determine_rate handler is implemented, the parent clock
and the actual clock are always computed and are applied by
clk_set_rate_no_lock(). Therefore the clock must implement .set_rate
handler instead of relying on CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT flag.

For cpu1/mpu clock it is not the case, so add the required ops set_rate()
to check the parent clock is the expected one after the call of
determine_rate().

Moreover for clocks with determine_rate ops, the flags CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT
is not needed (only used when determine_rate is absent), so we removes
this flags it when is possible.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 412bf635b760ccb577260f0153e970d01491a23c clk: stm32: fix management of set_rate and determine_rate]
